# RDE UI — Product Requirements

This is a React + TypeScript web app (Vite) that acts as a control center for a Remote Development Environment (RDE). It connects to an RDE host and surfaces key information through focused panels.

## Panels

### ⚙️ ServicesPanel — supervisorctl services
- List all `supervisorctl` services with their current status (running / stopped / fatal / etc.)
- Python version badge per service — fetched from `GET /api/supervisor/venvs` which reads `/opt/fundbox/venvs/<service>/bin/python3 --version`; keyed by the program name (part after `:` in `group:program`)
- Actions per service: **start**, **stop**, **restart**
- Services may belong to a supervisor group (`group:program` format); group them visually
- 📋 Logs button per service — dispatches `openLogFile` event pointing at `/opt/fundbox/logs/<program>.log`

### 📋 LogsPanel — log viewer
- Always visible to the right of the left slot regardless of which tab is active
- Fetch logs from `/opt/fundbox/logs/<service_name>.log` for supervisor services
- Fetch `docker logs` for Docker containers via synthetic paths `/docker/<name>`
- **follow** mode uses SSE (`GET /api/logs/stream`) for real-time streaming; **last N lines** uses HTTP POST (`/api/logs/tail`)
- When tailing multiple files, `tail` emits `==> /path/to/file <==` headers — parse these to attribute each line to its correct source file
- Each log line is prefixed with `[filename]` in the viewer so multiple open logs are distinguishable
- Provide a **search / filter** input that matches across all open log files
- Opened via `openLogFile` custom event (`{ file, serviceName }`) dispatched from `ServicesPanel` or `DockerPanel`

### 🐳 DockerPanel — Docker containers
- Lives in the same left slot as `ServicesPanel`, switched via the **⚙️ Services / 🐳 Docker** tabs at the top of `left-panel-wrapper`
- There is **no Docker toggle in `ConnectionBar`** — switching is done via the tabs only
- List all containers (running and stopped) with name, image, status, and ports
- Actions per container: **start**, **stop**, **restart**
- 📋 Logs button per container — dispatches `openLogFile` with synthetic path `/docker/<name>`; `LogsPanel` streams `docker logs --tail N <name>` via the server bridge
- Synthetic `/docker/<name>` paths are included in `GET /api/logs/list` so `LogsPanel` recognises them

### CommandPanel — shell command runner
- Allow the user to type and run arbitrary shell commands on the RDE
- Stream stdout / stderr output in real time, distinguishing the two streams

### SDKUpdatePanel
- Show available SDK / dependency updates for RDE-managed services

### GitChangesPanel
- Show git status / diff for repos on the RDE

## Layout

- The left slot is a `left-panel-wrapper` div in `App.tsx` containing:
  - A `left-panel-tabs` tab bar with **⚙️ Services** and **🐳 Docker** tabs
  - A `left-panel-content` div that renders either `ServicesPanel` or `DockerPanel` based on the active tab
- `LogsPanel` is always rendered to the right of the left slot
- Other panels (`CommandPanel`, `SDKUpdatePanel`, `GitChangesPanel`) are toggled via `ConnectionBar` and rendered after `LogsPanel`

## Deployment

- Repo lives on the RDE at `/opt/fundbox/rde-ui`
- The Node bridge (`server.js`) runs as a supervisord program `rde-ui`, configured in `deployment/rde/rde-ui.ini`
- Setup is handled by `deployment/rde/setup.sh` — installs npm deps, builds the frontend, patches nginx, and registers the supervisor program
- UI is served at `https://<rde-host>/rde-ui/` via nginx alias pointing at `dist/`

## Data & Transport

- All browser→RDE calls go through `window.electronAPI` (defined in `src/mock-electron-api.ts`)
- The bridge is a zero-dependency Node script (`server.js`) on the RDE, listening on `127.0.0.1:28000`
- **Primary transport is WebSocket** (`wss://<host>/rde-api/ws`) — a single persistent connection per browser tab, managed by `src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts`
  - Reconnects automatically with exponential backoff
  - Subscription-based push protocol — clients send `subscribe:<topic>` / `unsubscribe:<topic>`; server starts/stops push loops when subscriber count changes
  - Topics: `stats` (machine CPU/mem/disk/load, every 5s), `procs` (per-service CPU/mem, every 5s), `supervisor-status` (every 10s, also pushed immediately after any control action)
  - Log streaming: `logs:follow` / `logs:tail` / `logs:stop` messages over the same socket
- `procs` collection uses a single `sudo supervisorctl status all` call (PIDs are in the output) + one `ps -p pid1,pid2,...` — **never** spawn one subprocess per service
- HTTP REST remains for control actions and one-shot fetches:
  - `GET  /api/supervisor/status` — run `sudo supervisorctl status all`
  - `GET  /api/supervisor/venvs` — read Python version from each `/opt/fundbox/venvs/<name>/bin/python3`
  - `POST /api/supervisor/{start,stop,restart,bulk}` — control services
  - `GET  /api/logs/list` — returns log files + `/docker/<name>` synthetic paths
  - `POST /api/logs/tail` — one-shot last N lines (also available over WS as `logs:tail`)
  - `GET  /api/logs/stream` — SSE live stream kept for backwards-compat; prefer WS `logs:follow`
  - `POST /api/logs/stop` — kill an active stream
  - `GET  /api/docker/containers` — `docker ps -a`
  - `POST /api/docker/action` — `docker start/stop/restart`
- Nginx proxies `/rde-api/ws` with `Upgrade`/`Connection` headers; `/rde-api/logs/stream` with `proxy_buffering off`
- Types are defined in `src/types.ts` — extend there when adding new data shapes

## UX Rules

- `ConnectionBar` is the top-level toolbar; toggles for `CommandPanel`, `SDKUpdatePanel`, and `GitChangesPanel` live there — **not** the Docker/Services switch
- Use the `ToastContext` for transient success / error / info notifications (avoid alert/confirm)
- Support light and dark themes via `ThemeContext`
- Keyboard shortcuts are centralised in `useKeyboardShortcuts`


